      "text": "We will start by finding the area of the entire semicircle made up of arc $ADB$, and of arc $BEC$, as well as half of an additional semicircle made up of arc $DFE$. The base $AD$ will be attained using the Pythagorean Theorem and will measure $\\sqrt{2}$, and the base of arc $ADB$ will be $\\sqrt{2}-1$. That is, a base of $\\sqrt{2}$ and a height of 1. Thus, the area of the entire semicircle is $\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}+1)$.\nThe next step will be finding the area of the additional semicircle made up of arc $DFE$ using the base $DE$ measuring 1 and the height being $\\sqrt{2}-1$. The area of such semicircle is $\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1+1)=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2}$.\nIn order to find the area of the shaded region, we take away the area of the semicircle with base $\\sqrt{2}-1$, which is $\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}-1+1)=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2}$. The area of the shaded region will be $2-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2}$.",
